   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Extent of progress in for the development of a robust Information Systems and Decision Support as part of the &#x201c;Cambodian Environmental Management Information System&#x201d; (CEMIS).
2. Level of technical input/advice and other required support for the design of sustainable financing mechanisms effectiveness
3. Level of technical input/advice and other required support for Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) effectiveness</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1= Limited extent: initial function of CEMIS
2. 1= Limited effective: initial assessment and analysis 
3. 1= Limited effective: initial M&amp;E functioning</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2= Moderate extent: DGIS team conducted an inventory of existing spatial data to be used in ISDS and developed an open-source platform. 
2. 2= Moderate effective: examined existing revenue sources and gaps for protected area management and reviewed options for sustainable finance mechanism. 
3. 2= Moderate effective: Developed annual, semi-annual and quarterly work plans, M&amp;E and communication plans. Supported designing and completion of baseline survey questions and data collection, entry and analysis.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2= Moderate extent: Four multi-stakeholder consultation meetings were conducted in collaboration with UNDP-led Essential Life Support Areas (ELSA) initiative to discuss how an environmental monitoring system can be developed through integration of various spatial database to identify and monitor nature-based solutions for biodiversity, climate and sustainable development in Cambodia.

2. 2= Moderate effective: An initial work plan and schedules for sustainable financing work has been discussed with and agreed by the Ministry of Environment. Work is being focused on 1) Examination of existing revenue sources and gaps for protected area management in the country; 2) Review of existing economic valuation studies on specific ecosystems in CSLEP and identification of key ecosystems to be targeted under sustainable financing options; 3) Identification and prioritization of potential sustainable finance mechanisms and/or sources to mobilize financial resources.

3. 2= Moderate effective: A &#x201c;tracking tool&#x201d; has been developed and shared with the national consultants responsible for coordinating the implementation of each component to coordinate with their respective teams to fill the tracking tool with the relevant information and report back to the CSLEP/PIU.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2= Moderate extent
2. 2= Moderate effective
3. 2= Moderate effective</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2= Moderate extent:
&#x2022; A beta-version of CEMIS platform developed
&#x2022; Procurement completed and IT/Network System is installed
&#x2022; Agreement on three-tier models/products for the Information Spatial Decision Support System (ISDS) on Protected Area Zoning drafted

2. 2= Moderate effective: A set of preliminary action steps (roadmap) for priority sustainable finance mechanisms identified

3. 2= Moderate effective: A set of project M&amp;E requirements including Monitoring Effectiveness Tracking Tool (METT), projects beneficiaries&#x2019; satisfaction, job creation indicators and reporting drafted.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
